{"address":"230 E Victoria St","attributes":{"Ambience":{"casual":false,"classy":false,"divey":false,"hipster":false,"intimate":false,"romantic":false,"touristy":false,"trendy":false,"upscale":false},"BusinessParking":{"garage":false,"lot":false,"street":true,"valet":false,"validated":false},"Music":null,"OutdoorSeating":true,"RestaurantsGoodForGroups":false,"RestaurantsReservations":true,"RestaurantsTakeOut":true,"WiFi":"no"},"business_stars":4.0,"categories":"Restaurants, Vegetarian, French, Vegan, Seafood, Asian Fusion, Gluten-Free, American (New)","city":"Santa Barbara","hours":{"Friday":"17:30-22:0","Saturday":"17:30-22:0","Sunday":"17:30-21:0","Thursday":"17:30-21:0","Tuesday":"17:30-21:0","Wednesday":"17:30-21:0"},"name":"Spiritland Bistro","review_info":[{"review_date":"2012-08-02 01:04:35","review_stars":5.0,"review_text":"im very honest with these reviews- look at my other ones. i'm not going to make excuses for places but im also not going to forget to appreciate the little things... and this was one of the best vegan meals i have ever had... EVER had... they are not even entirely vegan which is the shocker- as most non vegan places believe a plate full of vegetables is what us vegans eat.. this place was truly imaginative, and provided me with a perfect four course meal..  yes, i, Shirley, said perfect... a rare thing indeed.
i really wanted to have this place cater my wedding, the second i realized every bite i had was magical, i was truly obsessed with the idea of them catering my wedding- and now that i'm planning it... they're gone. so sad.

wish places like this stayed open.... this and pure luck in silverlake... COME BACK PLEASE!"},{"review_date":"2012-03-01 05:20:25","review_stars":2.0,"review_text":"we'd been wanting to try this place for awhile... but when we finally did - underwhelmed.  the ambience would not have been so bad were there some music or lower lighting, but couldn't help but think, "i'm in a small room with 20 other people we don't know".  the food itself was ok, but not a special night out.  for $10 bucks a plate i would have gone back, but for $20 i'll go elsewhere."},{"review_date":"2011-12-31 16:54:19","review_stars":4.0,"review_text":"I called to make reservations for new years eve- this place is closed until further notice FYI. Not sure when they are planning to re-open."}],"state":"CA"}

{"address":"1014 Coast Village Rd","attributes":{"Ambience":{"casual":false,"classy":true,"divey":false,"hipster":false,"intimate":false,"romantic":false,"touristy":false,"trendy":false,"upscale":false},"BusinessParking":{"garage":false,"lot":true,"street":true,"valet":true,"validated":false},"Music":null,"OutdoorSeating":true,"RestaurantsGoodForGroups":true,"RestaurantsReservations":true,"RestaurantsTakeOut":true,"WiFi":"free"},"business_stars":4.5,"categories":"Restaurants, Italian, Pizza","city":"Santa Barbara","hours":{"Friday":"16:0-20:30","Monday":"0:0-0:0","Saturday":"16:0-20:30","Sunday":"16:0-20:30","Thursday":"16:0-20:30","Tuesday":"16:0-20:30","Wednesday":"16:0-20:30"},"name":"Bettina","review_info":[{"review_date":"2022-01-14 02:46:25","review_stars":1.0,"review_text":"The hype is over for this place. Local, who used to use this place for everything, and a spot to celebrate girlfriends birthdays. The food was not the issue. The staff is flat, unengaging and silent. You can feel their stuffy awkward energy. As someone who used to be a server myself, I always love being courteous to server staff/tipping well. But man, very hard to do here."},{"review_date":"2022-01-10 20:40:01","review_stars":5.0,"review_text":"Omg I'm a hard core pizza aficionado and this could be my new favorite pizza place in North America. Don't let it's location in the Montecito Country Mart fool you, please make a reservation asap. 

The menu is very tight but that's fine. Everyone raves about the carbonara pizza but I hate eggs do we skipped it. We wanted a light lunch to save room for steak dinner so we opted for a bottle of Sancerre, baby gems salad and meat lovers pizza. They all hit perfectly!

The server was terrific. The ambiance felt like a garden getaway and parking was too easy. Please run to this lovely restaurant and grab a matchbox or two for the memories."},{"review_date":"2022-01-06 05:51:02","review_stars":5.0,"review_text":"Decided to check out Bettina during our recent trip to Santa Barbara and boy was it a great experience. The location is random (in the Montecito country mart shopping center) but the inside and the courtyard of the restaurant are charming. And we figured we came to a good spot when we noticed all the locals either dining there or picking up pies. Everything we ordered was delicious! We got the burrata to start, that had this amazing green pistachio/veggie paste on top - it also came with an excellent Focaccia. Broccolini, which was tangy, charred to perfection and just delish.  And two pizzas, the mushroom and pepperoni, which may have been the best I've had. Great little spot in SB, highly recommend."}],"state":"CA"}

{"address":"1049 Casitas Pass Rd","attributes":{"Ambience":{"casual":true,"classy":false,"divey":null,"hipster":false,"intimate":false,"romantic":false,"touristy":false,"trendy":false,"upscale":false},"BusinessParking":{"garage":false,"lot":true,"street":false,"valet":false,"validated":false},"Music":null,"OutdoorSeating":true,"RestaurantsGoodForGroups":true,"RestaurantsReservations":false,"RestaurantsTakeOut":true,"WiFi":"free"},"business_stars":4.5,"categories":"Restaurants, Asian Fusion, Breakfast & Brunch, American (Traditional)","city":"Carpinteria","hours":{"Friday":"7:0-14:0","Saturday":"7:0-14:0","Sunday":"7:0-14:0","Thursday":"7:0-14:0","Tuesday":"7:0-14:0","Wednesday":"7:0-14:0"},"name":"Hugos Restaurant","review_info":[{"review_date":"2021-12-15 18:08:24","review_stars":4.0,"review_text":"We almost gave this place a pass - not a lot of upfront charm. But the Yelp reviews were good so we gave it a try. Glad we did! Friendly service as soon as we walked in. Basic breakfast was hot and delicious. I had scrambled eggs (fresh and yummy) with crispy hash browns and sourdough toast. My husband had the veggie scramble (zucchini, red peppers, onion, mushrooms) all fresh and delicious, with the same sides I had. Good cup of coffee, also! We appreciate a hard-working local restaurant and will definitely come back. Four stars just because the ambiance isn't really there. Don't let that stop you from giving this place a try!"},{"review_date":"2021-11-27 01:28:40","review_stars":5.0,"review_text":"We were coming home from a college visit trip to SLO and UCSB and wanted to hit Carp for breakfast. My kid typed in breakfast and this was one of the first that popped up - thank you Yelp!! Mom and pop-type small strip-mall cafe and we loved it. My wife and kids had pancakes (wife added blueberries) with eggs and I had the French toast. A side of hash browns to share (although we probably didn't need it) - just what the road trip ordered. Super friendly and when the people in front of us didn't need menus because the locals know what they want, it is a good sign. Hard working family, but open from 7am-2pm so it might not be a bad gig.... We will stop there again I am sure."},{"review_date":"2021-10-09 16:17:22","review_stars":5.0,"review_text":"Hugo's Restaurant in Carpinteria is THE best breakfast/brunch spot. I especially love their pancakes, stir fried noodles, and chilaquiles! Their menu is so diverse and anyone can find something to their liking. 

The owners are so welcoming and joyful every time I visit. They have been operating for 20+ years! The service is phenomenal; you never have to wait long for your food. 

If you're ever in the area, this is the spot."}],"state":"CA"}

{"address":"30 E Victoria St","attributes":{"Ambience":{"casual":null,"classy":null,"divey":false,"hipster":false,"intimate":null,"romantic":null,"touristy":false,"trendy":false,"upscale":false},"BusinessParking":{"garage":null,"lot":false,"street":true,"valet":false,"validated":false},"Music":null,"OutdoorSeating":null,"RestaurantsGoodForGroups":true,"RestaurantsReservations":true,"RestaurantsTakeOut":true,"WiFi":"no"},"business_stars":4.0,"categories":"Italian, Restaurants","city":"Santa Barbara","hours":{"Friday":"17:0-22:0","Saturday":"17:0-22:0","Sunday":"17:0-21:0","Thursday":"17:0-21:0","Tuesday":"17:0-21:0","Wednesday":"17:0-21:0"},"name":"Trattoria Vittoria","review_info":[{"review_date":"2022-01-09 04:55:39","review_stars":5.0,"review_text":"Great italian food. came here on a whim and thorough enjoyed it. will return next time i'm visiting santa barbara."},{"review_date":"2021-12-11 08:50:25","review_stars":5.0,"review_text":"Their homemade pasta dishes, lasagna, tortellini and ravioli with a heavenly tomato sauce was definitely one of the most delicious dishes I've tried (and then I've been to Italy). The servers where so funny and genuine, too. We'll be back in SB when we get the chance!"},{"review_date":"2021-12-08 17:23:35","review_stars":4.0,"review_text":"We had an early dinner here. It filled up fast so if you can make reservations you should. 

We had an awesome dinner. Atmosphere was perfect.  Wine was delicious and the service was great. 

Next time I will come early and have a drink at the bar. Looked like a fun crowd. Enjoy!"}],"state":"CA"}

{"address":"1180 University Ctr, Bldg 252","attributes":{"Ambience":{"casual":false,"classy":false,"divey":false,"hipster":false,"intimate":false,"romantic":false,"touristy":false,"trendy":false,"upscale":false},"BusinessParking":{"garage":false,"lot":false,"street":false,"valet":false,"validated":true},"Music":null,"OutdoorSeating":true,"RestaurantsGoodForGroups":true,"RestaurantsReservations":false,"RestaurantsTakeOut":true,"WiFi":"paid"},"business_stars":3.5,"categories":"Fast Food, Caterers, Chinese, Szechuan, Event Planning & Services, Restaurants","city":"Santa Barbara","hours":{"Friday":"10:0-17:0","Monday":"10:0-17:0","Thursday":"10:0-17:0","Tuesday":"10:0-17:0","Wednesday":"10:0-17:0"},"name":"Rice Garden","review_info":[{"review_date":"2013-06-08 01:53:14","review_stars":3.0,"review_text":"Its a shame, this place used to be so much better last year. They had a much wider variety last year. The curry chicken tasted almost like authentic chinese, and I enjoyed the Spicy Chicken every time. They switched around the menu, but usually they had 2 very good items everyday.

Now, its pretty much the same generic items everyday. On top of that, they are almost always sold out, whether because its rush lunch hour, or its after 2 or 3 and they just give up making half the menu.

I hear its getting replaced by Yoshinoya. I am glad because I love Yoshinoya."},{"review_date":"2013-03-07 21:26:31","review_stars":1.0,"review_text":"I would say the food was good if I could ever have it. Every time I go to this place they are "out" of what I want, nothing on deck, just simply out. Some times when I go they tell me that things are going to be done at exactly 1pm (which may be over 30 mins away)...its especially frustrating when these should be (and probably are) the money makers for the business. Teriyaki chicken? ITS CHICKEN, why is this not in abundance?? Why does the business run out of it!??! Why is there a 50 cents extra charge for the simplest menu item??! I can't make sense of it, I won't be going back, it is simply absurd."},{"review_date":"2012-10-05 21:11:32","review_stars":3.0,"review_text":"Best place to eat anywhere near UCSB. It's cheap, it tastes awesome, and the service is fast and good. Everything tastes fresh, unlike Panda Express. Too bad it's gone now."}],"state":"CA"}

{"address":"7018 Marketplace Dr","attributes":{"Ambience":{"casual":false,"classy":false,"divey":false,"hipster":false,"intimate":false,"romantic":false,"touristy":false,"trendy":false,"upscale":false},"BusinessParking":{"garage":false,"lot":true,"street":false,"valet":false,"validated":false},"Music":null,"OutdoorSeating":true,"RestaurantsGoodForGroups":true,"RestaurantsReservations":false,"RestaurantsTakeOut":true,"WiFi":"no"},"business_stars":4.0,"categories":"Donuts, Restaurants, Bakeries, Food, Sandwiches","city":"Goleta","hours":{"Friday":"6:0-17:30","Monday":"0:0-0:0","Saturday":"6:0-17:30","Sunday":"6:0-16:30","Thursday":"6:0-16:0","Tuesday":"6:0-17:30","Wednesday":"6:0-17:30"},"name":"Anna's Marketplace Bakery","review_info":[{"review_date":"2022-01-18 01:20:49","review_stars":4.0,"review_text":"Donuts are delish, nice and light and fresh. The chocolate croissant was really good as well! They are a little more pricey than some donut shops but have really good flavor."},{"review_date":"2022-01-01 18:44:53","review_stars":5.0,"review_text":"Happy 2022 everyone! This year will surely see me at Anna's quite a few more times. When a friend told me that a bakery close to where I live offers vegan donuts, I was psyched--I'm vegan and it's oddly difficult to find good vegan food, sweets, and drinks in this area. Checking out Anna's Bakery a few days later, I wasn't let down. 

I've sampled both the vegan glazed donut and the apple fritter, as well as the house coffee, and all were great. The donut is puffy and airy and sweet. The fritter has glorious crunchy, oily edges and a surprisingly doughy interior, complete with apple pieces and a glossy, sugary varnish. (Did you know some 'apple fritters' elsewhere don't even contain apple?) The coffee is hot and black and perfectly balances the candy-like sweetness of the baked goods. 

There's always a long line and seating is limited so be prepared. This shop also offers non-vegan donuts (the majority contain milk products, though I'm crossing my fingers for a vegan cake donut in 2022). There is also a menu of savory food. Breads and donuts and cookies are also available to go. That pink box, unmistakably brimming with tasty treats, is sure to being smiles to any gathering... especially if you have vegan friends who are so used to being left out when sweet baked goods appear."},{"review_date":"2021-10-27 05:28:12","review_stars":5.0,"review_text":"SO friendly and donuts are always amazing. All staff, from the cashier to the owner. All lovely people. They always greet with by my name. I love to see how they interact with all customers. I am always happy to give them business as it is very well deserved. Keep up the wonderful work! Anna's has been around for a long time and has always been one of my favorites."}],"state":"CA"}

{"address":"5711 Calle Real","attributes":{"Ambience":{"casual":true,"classy":false,"divey":false,"hipster":false,"intimate":false,"romantic":false,"touristy":false,"trendy":false,"upscale":false},"BusinessParking":{"garage":false,"lot":true,"street":false,"valet":false,"validated":false},"Music":null,"OutdoorSeating":true,"RestaurantsGoodForGroups":true,"RestaurantsReservations":true,"RestaurantsTakeOut":true,"WiFi":"free"},"business_stars":3.0,"categories":"American (New), Italian, Restaurants, Pizza","city":"Goleta","hours":{"Friday":"16:30-21:30","Monday":"16:30-21:0","Saturday":"16:30-21:0","Sunday":"16:30-21:0","Thursday":"16:30-21:0","Tuesday":"16:30-21:0","Wednesday":"16:30-21:0"},"name":"Petrini's Restaurant","review_info":[{"review_date":"2016-09-02 07:51:10","review_stars":5.0,"review_text":"I tend not to expect much from food locations in Strip Malls.  While staying in the Santa Barbara area, I just wanted a good piece of Pizza. We stopped here while on a walk and ordered an onion and cheese pizza, small size.  Neither of us could believe how fresh and great it was! The sauce was a good homemade red with Italian spices and fresh tomato flavor. Just enough good cheese.  We stopped in twice after having such great luck.  Tried the salads, pasta and more pizza, garlic bread and wine.  Family owned and run place that's cordial and homey.   This is the kind of place you find in Chicago and New York. Just a little gem with friendly people and really good Italian food!"},{"review_date":"2016-08-17 01:35:09","review_stars":1.0,"review_text":"Well, I tried eating at this Petrini's again, and I'm really sad to report that the food has gotten worse AND more expensive. The Chicken Picatta was drowning in butter, or grease; I'm not sure what that was. The fettuccine Alfredo that came with it was undercooked and had zero taste. We also were served garlic bread that was burned to black. To make things worse, I took the food home because I just could eat it at the restaurant. I was hungry later so I ate it. 
Oh My God.....I couldn't keep it down. I got such a stomach ache from that food. Petrini's , you are a local restaurant and I really try to support local businesses, but you are bad for my health."},{"review_date":"2016-07-11 15:51:04","review_stars":4.0,"review_text":"I have not been in here for many years, but we stopped in the other night and it was tasty traditional american italian food for a great price. The meat raviolis were very tender and delicious and the sauce was spot on. The spaghetti and meatballs (the yard stick for any italian review) were also very good. I also really enjoyed my cup of minestrone soup, really hit the spot. The waiters were very attentive and the place had a very welcoming and tidy atmosphere. 

The only downside, the water tasted horrible, I think they need to replace their filter or something."}],"state":"CA"}

{"address":"1429 San Andres St","attributes":{"Ambience":{"casual":null,"classy":null,"divey":true,"hipster":null,"intimate":null,"romantic":null,"touristy":null,"trendy":true,"upscale":false},"BusinessParking":{"garage":false,"lot":false,"street":true,"valet":false,"validated":false},"Music":null,"OutdoorSeating":true,"RestaurantsGoodForGroups":null,"RestaurantsReservations":null,"RestaurantsTakeOut":true,"WiFi":"free"},"business_stars":4.5,"categories":"Restaurants, Pizza","city":"Santa Barbara","hours":{"Friday":"16:0-22:0","Saturday":"16:0-22:0","Sunday":"16:0-22:0","Thursday":"16:0-22:0","Wednesday":"16:0-22:0"},"name":"Revolver","review_info":[{"review_date":"2022-01-06 20:15:13","review_stars":5.0,"review_text":"Nothing derails my good intentions of starting a diet like a Revolver Pizza craving! It's absolutely the BEST!! Beautifully handmade crust and fresh toppings. Not fancy just delicious. And the salads are incredible. Best Caesar with real anchovy dressing. Market salad has yummy dill ranch, shaved vegetables on yummy lettuce. I don't love the atmosphere, so we always get it to go. It's super popular so get your order in early! But it's definitely our favorite pizza in SB."},{"review_date":"2022-01-01 06:13:46","review_stars":4.0,"review_text":"Great pizza but limited toppings odd hours and long wait time for food.

They really should open at 11am like any other normal pizza place."},{"review_date":"2021-12-20 02:58:37","review_stars":5.0,"review_text":"Hands down the best dang pizza in all of Santa Barbara. Not even close. Simple menu and from the crisp on the crust and bottom to the tang in the red sauce, SB you have a winner. It's artisan pizza meets NY on the west coast. Proves you don't need to be in the funk zone to have something great and feels like Brooklyn back 20
Years ago in the fact that they are hip but hard working and making something great. The Caesar salad had a great dressing and fresh greens to boot."}],"state":"CA"}

{"address":"7020 Market Place Dr","attributes":{"Ambience":null,"BusinessParking":{"garage":false,"lot":true,"street":false,"valet":false,"validated":false},"Music":null,"OutdoorSeating":true,"RestaurantsGoodForGroups":true,"RestaurantsReservations":false,"RestaurantsTakeOut":true,"WiFi":null},"business_stars":2.5,"categories":"Restaurants, Japanese","city":"Goleta","hours":null,"name":"Mika","review_info":[{"review_date":"2011-08-31 03:46:28","review_stars":2.0,"review_text":"Had the Ai Roll Ai Roll, not very good... I mean it's edible and tastes okay.. but I don't think it justifies the price."},{"review_date":"2011-08-25 19:38:36","review_stars":1.0,"review_text":"Chicken bowl was disappointing. When I asked for white meat only they informed me that they only carry dark meat.... 

I consider myself to be pretty easy to please,considering my college budget, however I'm pretty sure I will never eat there again...unless forced.


I will not be returning, no matter what they change the name too."},{"review_date":"2011-08-11 15:30:57","review_stars":1.0,"review_text":"So I came with a group of co-workers after tring to figure out a place to eat. I was craving something somewhat healthy so I went with the Teriyaki chicken bowl. I asked for brown rice but they only serve white. the chicken tasted rubbery and they loaded they soaked the bowl with sauce. Even though it was only $6 bucks I wouldn't have spent a $1 on this! The service was extra slow and the staff wasn't friendly. I will not be back."}],"state":"CA"}

{"address":"1128 Chapala St","attributes":{"Ambience":{"casual":true,"classy":null,"divey":null,"hipster":null,"intimate":null,"romantic":null,"touristy":null,"trendy":null,"upscale":null},"BusinessParking":{"garage":false,"lot":false,"street":true,"valet":false,"validated":false},"Music":false,"OutdoorSeating":false,"RestaurantsGoodForGroups":true,"RestaurantsReservations":null,"RestaurantsTakeOut":null,"WiFi":null},"business_stars":4.0,"categories":"Nightlife, Pool Halls","city":"Santa Barbara","hours":{"Friday":"12:0-2:0","Monday":"12:0-2:0","Saturday":"12:0-2:0","Sunday":"12:0-2:0","Thursday":"12:0-2:0","Tuesday":"12:0-2:0","Wednesday":"12:0-2:0"},"name":"Don Q Family Billiard Center","review_info":[{"review_date":"2021-11-22 17:31:14","review_stars":4.0,"review_text":"I've been going to Don Q for 40+ years! While other pool halls have come and gone, Don Q has endured - I think they still have the same 70s-80s rock playlist in the jukebox. They have the highest quality tables and cloth, both bar and regulation size. It's fun and comfortable with the kids, a date, your wife or the guys - never feels seedy or uncomfortable. The beer and snack selection have increased greatly over time, and are downright over the top now. My only wishes: that they still had scoring beads for straight pool, some chalk cones, and didn't require the felt pad under the cue ball at break. Nonetheless, Don Q is the absolute best place to play pool in SB."},{"review_date":"2021-10-23 23:15:31","review_stars":1.0,"review_text":"this place is not a real billiards hall. the felt on all the pool tables is in  bad shape & when u ask the owner about it he'll just be rude.! stiix in ventura is where u have to go to play on real billiards tables. the only reason they r still open is because the kids know they can drink there !"},{"review_date":"2019-04-22 04:55:17","review_stars":1.0,"review_text":"The management at Don Q is probably the worst we've ever encountered in any business venue. We visited there after speaking to someone over the phone to discuss a possible opportunity for a large party event. The venue was relatively full but not overwhelming and the individual in charge couldn't take even a minute to talk to us complaining he was too busy; and, he even avoided us even though we waited for a possible 5 minutes of his time. 

Along side this extreme rudeness, the venue allows outside food to be brought in. It wreaked of uncovered food throughout the place. Food on every counter and bar stool. Quite gross. 

I have to say I will never visit Don Q's again. Management is the rudest I've ever encountered and the place smells. They have a lot to learn about running a business and they missed out on a lucrative opportunity."}],"state":"CA"}

{"address":"6583 Pardall Rd","attributes":{"Ambience":{"casual":true,"classy":true,"divey":false,"hipster":false,"intimate":false,"romantic":false,"touristy":false,"trendy":false,"upscale":false},"BusinessParking":{"garage":false,"lot":true,"street":false,"valet":false,"validated":false},"Music":null,"OutdoorSeating":true,"RestaurantsGoodForGroups":true,"RestaurantsReservations":false,"RestaurantsTakeOut":true,"WiFi":"free"},"business_stars":4.5,"categories":"Restaurants, Chicken Wings, Sandwiches, Breakfast & Brunch, Pizza, Burgers","city":"Goleta","hours":{"Friday":"11:30-22:0","Monday":"0:0-0:0","Saturday":"17:0-22:0","Sunday":"11:0-22:0","Thursday":"11:30-22:0","Tuesday":"11:30-22:0","Wednesday":"11:30-19:0"},"name":"Rockfire Grill","review_info":[{"review_date":"2022-01-09 19:02:34","review_stars":5.0,"review_text":"Was a nice place good food and good service . Highly recommend. Lots of tvs for sports fans and overall good vibe"},{"review_date":"2022-01-05 05:57:43","review_stars":4.0,"review_text":"I really like Rockfire Grill. We were coming from LA  and stopped by there to grab something to eat. We got pizza, burger, and gyros. My daughter liked the burger. I liked all the food. Our pizza was  burnt at the bottom but they gladly renewed. Great customer service"},{"review_date":"2022-01-04 23:13:41","review_stars":5.0,"review_text":"My friend and I stopped in here to grab an outdoor dinner on a beautiful evening and we had a great experience! The patio has plenty of seating, service at the counter and efficient and our cashier gave great recommendations since we had never eaten here before. Loved the vibe, with the kind of surfy decor and a playlist that took me back to the Caribbean.

Let me start with the stars of the meal...the flatbread burger. Why aren't these a thing everywhere because they should be?! I ordered the East Bay BBQ and holy cow was it amazing. Meat was cooked to perfection, the house spread was something special, and the flatbread it came on was so good I basically have no words. My friend got the West Coast and she had the same reaction I did. We stuffed ourselves because it was so tasty. We also had chicken wings (with an absolutely delicious honey garlic sauce) and seasoned fries, both of which perfectly complemented the flatbread burgers.

I would order this whole meal again exactly the same way it was so good. Only wish we had one where I live (hint hint guys, open some more locations further down in SoCal). Already planning to take my boyfriend here next time we take a little day trip up to SB."}],"state":"CA"}

{"address":"103 Sant Felicia Dr","attributes":{"Ambience":null,"BusinessParking":null,"Music":null,"OutdoorSeating":null,"RestaurantsGoodForGroups":null,"RestaurantsReservations":null,"RestaurantsTakeOut":true,"WiFi":null},"business_stars":4.5,"categories":"Food, Restaurants, Mediterranean, Farmers Market, Specialty Food, Organic Stores, Street Vendors","city":"Goleta","hours":{"Friday":"8:0-17:0","Monday":"8:0-16:0","Thursday":"8:0-16:0","Tuesday":"8:0-16:0","Wednesday":"8:0-16:0"},"name":"Baba Small Batch","review_info":[{"review_date":"2020-04-04 19:13:09","review_stars":5.0,"review_text":"OK, to be honest, I stopped by the Baba stand at the Morro Bay farmers market, not because of the hummus. It was because of the wonderful red-headed gal that was working your booth. She turned out to be charming, helpful and informative. I had never tried hummus before. She explained it to me and helped me choose just the right one. I ended up buying 2 the first week and many more since then. Last week she talked me into trying the bread and I'm glad she did. I love her and I love your product.
Employees like her are hard to find. (I'm really bad with names or I would add it)"},{"review_date":"2018-08-31 07:15:44","review_stars":5.0,"review_text":"This has to be the best hummus I've ever had and the chips are an added bonus!! They have so many hummus flavors to choose from. Seriously this stuff is compared to drugs. Once you have a taste it, you can't stop. Haha. For the past few years they would make their way up to Fresno's River Park Farmers Market. But sad to say, they didn't come up this year. I'm sure everyone who bought their hummus here in town was saddened when  Baba's hummus didn't make an appearance. I know my family and I were sad. 

I hope I find their hummus when I go to SLO next weekend. If the owner is reading this, please come back to Fresno and sell your amazing hummus!"},{"review_date":"2017-07-07 05:28:45","review_stars":5.0,"review_text":"The baba spicy pepper with Harrisa is soooo good! It's a bit spicy so try it before you buy if you can't handle heat. But if you can give it a go. It's amazing."}],"state":"CA"}

